WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:02.200
- [Kelly] How do you
celebrate Thanksgiving?

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:03.910
- We usually have a big Thanksgiving,

00:00:03.910 --> 00:00:05.390
maybe for 40 people or so.

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:06.735
Everybody wants to come to my house

00:00:06.735 --> 00:00:09.240
'cause I raise my own turkeys.

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:10.520
- Sure.

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:12.040
- We have heritage breeds.

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:13.740
Do you know what heritage
breed turkeys are?

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:14.790
- No, but I'm sure they taste great.

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:18.136
- They are really good.
(audience laughs)

00:00:18.136 --> 00:00:20.530
I do turkeys three different ways.

00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:21.710
- You do three different turkeys?

00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:23.510
- Oh yeah, three different ways.

00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:26.313
- I love that you said "Oh
yeah" like that's normal.

00:00:26.313 --> 00:00:28.000
- For 40 people you need three turkeys.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.010
- Okay, I got you.
- They're 25 pounds each.

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:33.060
We're doing a turkey wrapped in parchment

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:37.520
so you start off baking
it at a low temperature

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:38.520
and then you raise the temperature

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:39.790
and when you take the paper off

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:41.653
- My mouth is watering.
- it gets all nice

00:00:41.653 --> 00:00:43.200
and glossy brown skin.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.670
- I bet your turkey's the jam.

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:47.030
- Then we got spatchcock turkey.

00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:48.500
Ever do a spatchcock?
- What?

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:49.440
- I'm just realizing that there are

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:51.111
three different ways to do turkey.

00:00:51.111 --> 00:00:51.944
(audience laughs)

00:00:51.944 --> 00:00:53.857
I'm still stuck on three right now.

00:00:53.857 --> 00:00:54.690
- What did you say,

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:55.523
a spatch?
- There are many more

00:00:55.523 --> 00:00:56.633
than three ways, spatchcock.

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:00.080
It's nothing dirty, it's nothing dirty.

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:02.640
- It doesn't sound it.
- It means split the cock.

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:04.143
The Hocklets of a rooster.

00:01:06.978 --> 00:01:07.991
(audience applauds)
It used to be--

00:01:07.991 --> 00:01:10.184
- Somebody's gotta do it.
- It used to be about chicken.

00:01:10.184 --> 00:01:12.313
- Somebody's gotta do it, Martha.

00:01:12.313 --> 00:01:14.500
- What it means is you
take out the backbone

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:17.840
with a pair of scissors
and you spread it flat

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:20.812
and it cooks in a third of the time.

00:01:20.812 --> 00:01:21.645
- Oh!

00:01:21.645 --> 00:01:24.820
- So for those of you who are oven poor,

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:26.570
you only have one oven,
you have to bake the pies,

00:01:26.570 --> 00:01:28.250
you have to do all the sides,
you have to do the turkey.

00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:30.274
- I love that you said over poor.

00:01:30.274 --> 00:01:32.578
Most houses have one oven.

00:01:32.578 --> 00:01:34.606
(laughing)

00:01:34.606 --> 00:01:36.606
I love it, it's amazing.

00:01:37.490 --> 00:01:38.960
I want your life.

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:39.913
So you have a show

00:01:39.913 --> 00:01:40.746
with Snoop Dogg.
- Once sip of wine

00:01:40.746 --> 00:01:42.070
and I'm already giddy.
- Oh, me too.

00:01:42.070 --> 00:01:43.003
I'm a lightweight.

